decision_details_body:
- The Members of Parliament elected by the people, the Ministers and the former Presidents have been provided with different entitlements, allowances and privileges such as salaries, allowances, pensions, official quarters, vehicles, staff, office equipment, security personnel etc. The Government has to incur a considerable cost from the public taxes for the provision of said entitlements, allowances and privileges and it has been found the need to reduce this huge expenses within the existing fiscal space. Accordingly, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in her capacity as the Minister of Justice, Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils, Local Government and Labour to appoint a Committee with the following composition, to examine the matters in that regard and submit a Report with appropriate recommendations within two (02) months to limit the irrational entitlements, allowances and privileges which are causing an unnecessary burden to the General Treasury on a rational basis or to introduce other suitable alternative methodologies:

*	Justice K.T. Chitrasiri - (Chairman),
  	Retired Judge of the Supreme Court;

*	Mr. D. Dissanayake,
  	Retired Ministry Secretary;

*	Mrs. Jayantha C.T. Bulumulla,
  	Retired District Secretary/Government Agent;

- 2023-03-09 දින පැවැත්වීමට නියමිතව තිබූ පළාත් පාලන ආයතන ඡන්ද විමසීම දින නියමයක් නොමැතිව කල් යාම හේතු කොට ගෙන 2024 වර්ෂයේ අලුත් කරන ලද ඡන්ද හිමියන්ගේ නාම ලේඛනයෙහි නම ඇතුළත්ව ඇති 900,000කට අධික ඡන්ද දායක පිරිසකට ඉදිරි පළාත් පාලන ආයතන ඡන්ද විමසීමේදී ඡන්දය ලබා දීම සහ ඡන්ද අපේක්ෂකත්වය ලැබීමට ඇති අයිතිවාසිකම අහිමි වී යාමට ඉඩ ඇති බව පෙනී ගොස් ඇත. ආණ්ඩුක්‍රම ව්‍යවස්ථාවේ 4 වන ව්‍යවස්ථාව ප්‍රකාරව වයස අවුරුදු 18ක් සම්පූර්ණ වී ඇති, ඡන්ද හිමියෙකුවීමට සුදුසුකම් ලැබ තමාගේ නම ඡන්ද හිමි නාම ලේඛනයේ ඇතුළත් කරනු ලැබ ඇති සෑම පුරවැසියෙකුටම සිය ඡන්ද බලය ක්‍රියාත්මක කිරීමට හැකි විය යුතු නමුත්, ඉදිරියේදී පැවැත්වීමට නියමිත පළාත් පාලන ආයතන ඡන්ද විමසීම සඳහා 2023 ජනවාරි මස නාම යෝජනා කැඳවා අවසන් වී ඇති බැවින් එකී නාම යෝජනා මත පවත්වනු ලබන ඡන්ද විමසීමේදී ඡන්දය ප්‍රකාශ කළ හැක්කේ එතෙක් ලියාපදිංචිව සිටි ඡන්ද දායකයින්ට පමණක් බවට නිරීක්ෂණය වී ඇත. එසේම, 2023 අංක 30 දරන පළාත් පාලන ආයතන ඡන්ද විමසීම් (සංශෝධන) පනත සම්මත වීමෙන් පසුව පළාත් පාලන ආයතන සඳහා ඉදිරිපත් කරනු ලබන නාම යෝජනා පත්‍රවල 25%ක තරුණ නියෝජනයක් සඳහා අවකාශ සැලසීම සිදු කළ යුතුව ඇත. එහෙත්, මේ වන විට 2023 වර්ෂයේදී නාම යෝජනා කැඳවා තිබීම හේතුවෙන් තරුණ ප්‍රජාව සඳහා 25%ක අනිවාර්ය අවස්ථාව මග හැරී ගොස්  තිබේ. එබැවින් -

	*	ඉදිරියේදී පැවැත්වීමට නියමිත පළාත් පාලන ආයතන ඡන්ද විමසීමේදී ඡන්ද හිමි නාම ලේඛනයේ නම ඇතුළත්ව ඇති එහෙත් ඡන්දය ප්‍රකාශ කිරීමට නොහැකි වී ඇති ඡන්ද දායකයින්ගේ ඡන්දය ප්‍රකාශ කිරීමේ අයිතිවාසිකම් ආරක්ෂා කරලීම සඳහා ද;

	*	2024 ඡන්ද හිමි නාම ලේඛනයේ නම සඳහන් තරුණ ඡන්ද දායකයින් 900,000කට වැඩි පිරිසකට ඡන්ද අපේක්ෂකයෙකු ලෙස ඡන්දය සඳහා ඉදිරිපත් වීමේ මූලික අයිතිවාසිකම් අහිමි වී යාමට ඉඩ ඇති බැවින් එකී අයිතිවාසිකම් ආරක්ෂා කරලීම සඳහා ද;

	*	2023 අංක 30 දරන පළාත් පාලන ආයතන ඡන්ද විමසීම් (සංශෝධන) පනතේ විධිවිධාන ප්‍රකාරව ඡන්ද අපේක්ෂකයෙකු ලෙස ඉදිරිපත් වීමේදී තරුණයින් සඳහා වන කෝටාව අහිමි වී යාම හේතුවෙන් අසාධාරණයට ලක් විය හැකි තරුණ ප්‍රජාවගේ අයිතිවාසිකම් ආරක්ෂා කරදීම සඳහා ද;

2023 පළාත් පාලන ආයතන ඡන්ද විමසීම සඳහා කැඳවා ඇති නාම යෝජනා ආපසු කැඳවීමටත්, ඉන් අනතුරුව 2024 ඡන්ද නාම ලේඛනය පදනම් කර ගෙන පළාත් පාලන ආයතන ඡන්ද විමසීම පැවැත්වීම සඳහා නැවත නාම යෝජනා කැඳවීමටත් මැතිවරණ කොමිෂන් සභාව වෙත අවශ්‍ය බලතල ලැබෙන පරිදි, එකී කොමිෂන් සභාව විමසමින්, යෝග්‍ය විධිවිධාන ඇතුළත්ව පළාත් පාලන ආයතන ඡන්ද විමසීම් (විශේෂ විධිවිධාන) පනත් කෙටුම්පතක් සකස් කරන ලෙස නීති කෙටුම්පත් සම්පාදක වෙත උපදෙස් ලබා දීම පිණිස රාජ්‍ය පරිපාලන, ස්වදේශ කටයුතු, පළාත් සභා හා පළාත් පාලන අමාත්‍ය වශයෙන් ගරු අග්‍රාමාත්‍යතුමා සහ අධිකරණ, බන්ධනාගාර කටයුතු හා ආණ්ඩුක්‍රම ව්‍යවස්ථා ප්‍රතිසංස්කරණ අමාත්‍යතුමා ඉදිරිපත් කළ ඒකාබද්ධ යෝජනාව අමාත්‍ය මණ්ඩලය විසින් අනුමත කරන ලදී.

- Due to the indefinite postponement of the Local Authorities Election scheduled to be held on 2023‑03‑09, it has appeared that over 900,000 voters whose names have been included in the Register of Electors updated in the year 2024 are likely to be deprived of their right to vote and to be an election candidature at the upcoming Local Authorities Election. In terms of Article 4 of the Constitution, although, every citizen who has attained 18 years of age and whose name has been entered in the Register of Electors being eligible to be a voter, should be able to exercise his franchise, it has been observed that since calling for nominations for the Local Authorities Election to be held in future has been concluded in January 2023, only voters then registered could cast their votes at the election to be conducted on the said nominations. Similarly, subsequent to the passage of the Local Authorities Election (Amendment) Act No. 30 of 2023, it is required to provide the opportunity for 25% of youth representation in the nomination papers submitted for Local Authorities. Nevertheless, due to the fact that nominations have been called in the year 2023 as of now, 25% of mandatory opportunity for the youth community have been prevented. Therefore, the joint proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils and Local Government and the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Local Authorities Elections (Special Provisions) Bill incorporating the appropriate provisions in consultation with the Election Commission so as to receive the necessary authority for the said Commission to re-call for nominations called for the Local Authorities Election 2023 and thereafter to call for nominations to conduct the Local Authorities Election based on the Register of Electors in the year 2024 for - 

      *	protecting the right to vote of the voters whose names have been 	included in the Register of Electors but who have been unable to cast 	their vote at the upcoming Local Authorities Election;

      *	protecting the fundamental right of over 900,000 of voters who are 	youth whose names are included in the 2024 Register of Electors, 	who are likely to be deprived of their right to come forward to 	contest as a candidate at the Election;

      *	protecting the rights of the youth community that may subjected to 	injustice due to deprivation of the quota in contesting as a candidate in 	the Election in terms of the provisions in the Local Authorities Elections 	(Amendment) Act, No.30 of 2023;

was approved by the Cabinet.

- Under the the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act, No. 11 of 2021, it is required to designate the Authorized Persons as Secondary Business of Strategic Importance and to publish the exemptions or incentives proposed for such designated businesses  in the Gazette through an Order and thereafter submit the said Orders in Parliament for information. Accordingly, the proposals made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Investment Promotion to submit the Orders under section 53 of the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act, No. 11 of 2021 published through the following Gazette Notifications to Parliament, were approved by the Cabinet. 

*	the Order published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2394/06 dated 2024‑07‑22;

*	the Order published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2394/09 dated 2024‑07‑22;

*	the Order published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2394/10 dated 2024‑07‑22;

*	the Order published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2394/11 dated 2024‑07‑22;

*	the Order published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2394/12 dated 2024‑07‑22;

*	the Order published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2394/13 dated 2024‑07‑22;

*	the Order published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2394/14 dated 2024‑07‑22;

*	the Order published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2394/15 dated 2024‑07‑22;

*	the Order published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2394/16 dated 2024‑07‑22; 

*	the Order published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification        No.2394/17 dated 2024‑07‑22;

*	the Order published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification                               No.2394/07 dated 2024‑07‑22;

*	the Order published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2394/08 dated 2024‑07‑22; and

*	the Order published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2394/18 dated 2024‑07‑22.

- Approval of Parliament is required to obtain within the period specified in the Special Commodity Levy Act, No.48 of 2007 for the Orders published in the Gazette in order to enforce the amendments of the Special Commodity Levy which is imposed in the importation of certain selected commodities under the said Act. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to submit the Orders published through the following Gazette Extraordinary Notifications under the Special Commodity Levy Act, No.48 of 2007, to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet:

*	the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2360/52 dated 2023‑11‑30;

*	the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2365/04 dated 2024‑01‑02;

*	the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2365/84 dated 2024‑01‑07;

*	the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2372/06 dated 2024‑02‑19; and 

*	the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2373/42 dated 2024‑03‑01.

- Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to present the Orders/Regulations/Notifications made under the following Acts and published through the respective Gazette Notifications, for approval in Parliament:

*	the Order issued under the Excise (Special Provisions) Act, No.13 of 1989 and published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2364/36 dated 2023‑12‑31;

*	the Order issued under the Ports and Airports Development Levy Act, No.18 of 2011 and published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2364/37 dated 2023‑12‑31;

*	the Orders issued under the Finance Act, No.25 of 2003 and published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notifications No.2369/27 and No.2374/19 dated 2024‑02‑01 and 2024‑03‑06 respectively;

*	the Notification issued under the Finance Act, No.35 of 2018 (Luxury Tax on Motor Vehicles) and published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2368/24 dated 2024‑01‑24;

*	the Regulations issued under the Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka Act, No.19 of 2021 and published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2366/34 dated 2024‑01‑12;
